{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "The legacy predicate adds a categorical relief exclusion to a provision expressly preserving application processing. That interpretation is plausible, but its duration and treatment of withdrawal, replacement or resolution are not established.",
    "The formula preserves the explicit commencement date. Selection of the legally relevant assessment event remains unresolved; acknowledging that uncertainty does not resolve it operationally.",
    "The relevant FAQs, applicable home-jurisdiction requirements and existing approval process are missing. Neither unbound dependency ID has identifying metadata permitting a reliable match; neither has a non-null source_hash.",
    "Legal classifications are supplied inputs. The formula does not establish home-jurisdiction compliance or determine novelty, complexity or possible local policy implications.",
    "A false result does not establish an approval duty. A true result does not establish satisfaction of notification, filing or post-vetting requirements. These limits appropriately constrain the proposed permission.",
    "The supported date and independent local-policy exception can be assessed separately from missing implementation guidance. Their preservation does not establish overall legal correctness."
  ],
